    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "yeah that makes sense. it's just hard to tell sometimes since the infection is basically invisible until it's too late. is there anything else i should know about how pathogens or bacteria can just... hide in there and cause trouble without being noticed right away?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Indeed, ruminal bacteria can fluctuate in numbers rapidly and produce volatile metabolites that can be toxic even at low concentrations. Subtle shifts might not always have immediate visible signs but could precipitate a cascade of disturbances within the rumen. Monitoring pathogens and bacterial imbalances can be refined through rumen fluid analysis, which allows veterinarians or experienced technicians to evaluate the microbial profile and detect early signs of dysbiosis or infections that aren't externally apparent. Additionally, incorporating good husbandry practices and ensuring that your heifer doesn't experience stress or conveyer setbacks can help maintain a balanced rumen environment, which in turn, can help mitigate the risks of unseen rumen disturbances. Always stay vigilant, consult with professionals if any anomalies arise, and proactively address husbandry-related risk factors.",
      "source": "target",
      "gen_token_ids": [
        110355,
        11,
        15477,
        1028,
        32829,
        665,
        179851,
